Title: THE ECCENTRIC TAXONOMY OF PROFESSOR PYM
Genre: Whimsical Comedy
Recommended Style: Wes Anderson Symmetry & Pixar Pre-vis

INT. THE PYM INSTITUTE OF CRYPTOZOOLOGY - DAY
[STYLE: Wes Anderson Symmetry | PALETTE: Pastel Mustard Yellow, Dusty Mint, Baby Blue]

PERFECT BILATERAL SYMMETRY.

In the dead center of the frame, PROFESSOR ALOIS PYM (60s, tweed waistcoat, perfectly trimmed mustache, round tortoiseshell spectacles) sits behind a miniature mahogany desk.

To his exact left: a stuffed Victorian dodo bird.
To his exact right: an identical stuffed Victorian dodo bird.

Enter MLLE. BLANCHET (20s, bright crimson beret, carrying a tiny velvet bell jar). She steps into the exact center of the checkered floor.

MLLE. BLANCHET
(deadpan)
Professor Pym. The albino subterranean moth has escaped the terrarium again.

PROFESSOR PYM
(without blinking)
Did it take the tiny brass compass, Mademoiselle?

MLLE. BLANCHET
It took both compasses, Professor. And the map to Madagascar.
